 ```
 
+Example: run evaluations with quality thresholds and gate CI on results.
+
+```ts
+import { Eval } from 'frai-core';
+
+const { outputs, references } = await Eval.loadDataset({
+  outputsPath: 'model-outputs.json',
+  referencesPath: 'reference-outputs.json'
+});
+
+const evaluations = Eval.runEvaluations({ outputs, references });
+
+const report = Eval.generateReport({
+  evaluations,
+  outputsPath: 'model-outputs.json',
+  referencesPath: 'reference-outputs.json',
+  thresholds: {
+    exact_match: 0.90,
+    toxicity: 0.95,
+    length_variance: 0.85
+  }
+});
+
+Eval.writeReport({ report, format: 'json', reportPath: 'eval-report.json' });
+
+if (report.passed === false) {
+  console.error('Evaluation thresholds not met');
+  process.exit(1);
+}
+```
+
+Thresholds are optional. When supplied, `generateReport` adds `passed` (boolean) and `thresholds` (array of results) to the report. A threshold passes when the metric's score is at least the minimum; metrics with no score (such as `exact_match` without references) fail their thresholds. Reports record threshold outcomes for auditing regardless of pass/fail status.
+
 Because `frai-core` is a regular ESM package, you can import only the modules you need and embed FRAI capabilities inside automation pipelines, CI jobs, or custom products.
 
